# Mercure Hub - Production Environment
# Local copy: `task setup` creates .env.prod from this file; edit the copy.
# Used with: Caddyfile (Caddy terminates TLS).
#
# Set every empty value before deploying.
# Mercure will fail to start without valid JWT configuration. For JWKS-only
# verification, set MERCURE_ISSUER_MODE=jwks plus MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWKS_URI and
# MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWKS_URI (literal URLs); the static JWT keys are then unused.

# === Secrets (REQUIRED - set in deployment) ===
# MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_ALG / MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_ALG default to HS256 for a
# plain secret. A PEM-encoded key needs its algorithm set explicitly (for
# example RS256, ES256 or EdDSA); the hub refuses to start without it.
MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_KEY=""
MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_KEY=""

# Trusted issuer: the `iss` claim access tokens must carry (RFC 9068), bound to
# the two keys above (or the JWKS URLs in jwks mode). Must equal the tokens'
# `iss` in both modes. Defaults to https://localhost, which suits local
# development only. Set it to the stable identifier of your token issuer.
# It takes exactly one identifier and must not be set to an empty value; add
# more issuers in MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES.
# MERCURE_TRUSTED_ISSUERS=https://your-issuer.example.com

# === Server ===
SERVER_NAME=""

# Hub identifier: selects the per-hub health endpoint paths and the transport pool key.
# Customize per deployment (e.g., mercure-prod-us-east, mercure-prod-eu-west).
MERCURE_HUB_NAME=mercure-prod

# === Mercure Directives ===
# Defaults used: heartbeat 40s, write_timeout 600s (don't declare defaults)
#
# === Transport Selection ===
# The "transport" directive inside MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES controls which
# backend the hub uses. Swap by replacing the transport block.
# If no transport is specified, the hub defaults to bolt.
#
# Available transports:
#   bolt  — BoltDB, persistent, single-node (default for production)
#   local — in-memory, no persistence (not for production)
#   redis — Redis Streams, persistent, multi-node
MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES="
cors_origins
publish_origins
transport bolt {
    path ./data/bolt.db
}"
# To switch to redis transport, replace the transport block above with:
#   transport redis {
#       url redis://your-redis-host:6379
#       stream mercure
#       max_length 100000
#       encoding json
#       event_ttl 72h
#       cleanup_interval 5m
#   }
#
# To also trust an authorization server that publishes a JWKS, add an extra
# `issuer` block inside MERCURE_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES above (its identifier must
# differ from MERCURE_TRUSTED_ISSUERS). In the default `keys` mode the default
# issuer still needs its static keys above: leaving them empty makes the hub
# refuse to start. For a JWKS-only deploy, use MERCURE_ISSUER_MODE=jwks instead.
# issuer https://your-auth-server {
# 	publisher {
# 		jwks_uri https://your-auth-server/.well-known/jwks.json
# 	}
# 	subscriber {
# 		jwks_uri https://your-auth-server/.well-known/jwks.json
# 	}
# }

# === Caddy Global Options ===
GLOBAL_OPTIONS=""

# === Caddy Server Directives ===
CADDY_EXTRA_CONFIG=""
CADDY_SERVER_EXTRA_DIRECTIVES=""
